IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cp3-nouns`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part II -- INTERPRETATION (section 42) AND THE PENSION INDEX (section 43).
--
-- Section 42(1) defines the words of Part II; section 42(2) says when a person is disabled and from
-- what time; section 43 says how the Pension Index is worked out. Meanings that a regulation or
-- another Act gives (school or university, maintaining a child, the Divorce Act's decision-making
-- responsibility, the prescribed manner of a determination) are not in the texts this piece reads,
-- or belong to another piece (the Regulations' Part V is piece cr2): each is a plain input here,
-- named after the fact, with the regulation it comes from in a comment.
-- Ages go through section 2(2) of the Act (cpp-core-age.l4): the test is "has the person been
-- treated as reaching the age", never a subtraction of years.

§ `Part II -- Interpretation (section 42)`

§§ `42(1) -- the basic number of contributory months`

-- src:926 | basic number of contributory months, in the case of any contributor, means one hundred and twenty minus the number of months that were excluded from the contributor’s contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability; (nombre de base des mois cotisables)
@ref Act s 42(1) "basic number of contributory months" (src:926)
GIVEN `months excluded from the contributor's contributory period by reason of disability` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 42(1) — the basic number of contributory months` `months excluded from the contributor's contributory period by reason of disability` MEANS
    120 MINUS `months excluded from the contributor's contributory period by reason of disability`

§§ `42(1) -- child, dependent child, disabled contributor's child, orphan`

-- src:927 | child of a contributor means a child of the contributor, whether born before or after the contributor’s death, and includes
-- src:928 | (a) an individual adopted legally or in fact by the contributor while the individual was under twenty-one years of age, and
-- src:929 | (b) an individual in respect of whom, either legally or in fact, the contributor had, or immediately before the individual reached 21 years of age did have, parenting time or decision-making responsibility,
-- src:930 | but does not include a child of the contributor who is adopted legally or in fact by someone other than the contributor or the contributor’s spouse or common-law partner prior to the death or disability of the contributor, unless the contributor was maintaining the child, as defined by regulation; (enfant)
@ref Act s 42(1) "child of a contributor" (src:927-930)
GIVEN `the individual is a child of the contributor, whether born before or after the contributor's death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual was adopted legally or in fact by the contributor while under twenty-one years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor had, or immediately before the individual reached 21 years of age did have, parenting time or decision-making responsibility in respect of the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual was adopted legally or in fact by someone other than the contributor or the contributor's spouse or common-law partner before the contributor's death or disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor was maintaining the child, as defined by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: the contributor's own child, or a person adopted by the contributor before 21, or a
-- person the contributor looked after (parenting time or decision-making responsibility, as the
-- Divorce Act defines the latter); but not a child adopted by a stranger before the contributor's
-- death or disability, unless the contributor was maintaining the child (regulation 65.1, piece cr2).
-- out of range: regulation 65.1 (piece cr2): whether the contributor was maintaining the child is taken as a fact.
-- out of range: subsection 2(1) of the Divorce Act (another statute, not among the inputs): parenting time and decision-making responsibility are taken as facts.
`s 42(1) — a child of a contributor` `the individual is a child of the contributor, whether born before or after the contributor's death` `the individual was adopted legally or in fact by the contributor while under twenty-one years of age` `the contributor had, or immediately before the individual reached 21 years of age did have, parenting time or decision-making responsibility in respect of the individual` `the individual was adopted legally or in fact by someone other than the contributor or the contributor's spouse or common-law partner before the contributor's death or disability` `the contributor was maintaining the child, as defined by regulation` MEANS
        (   `the individual is a child of the contributor, whether born before or after the contributor's death`
         OR `the individual was adopted legally or in fact by the contributor while under twenty-one years of age`
         OR `the contributor had, or immediately before the individual reached 21 years of age did have, parenting time or decision-making responsibility in respect of the individual`)
    AND (   NOT `the individual was adopted legally or in fact by someone other than the contributor or the contributor's spouse or common-law partner before the contributor's death or disability`
         OR `the contributor was maintaining the child, as defined by regulation`)

-- src:931 | decision-making responsibility has the same meaning as in subsection 2(1) of the Divorce Act; (responsabilités décisionnelles)
-- src:947 | parenting time means the time that a child spends in the care of a person who is a parent of the child, who stands in the place of a parent or who intends to stand in the place of a parent, whether or not the child is physically with that person during that entire time; (temps parental)
@ref Act s 42(1) "parenting time" (src:947)
GIVEN `the child spends the time in the care of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a parent of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person stands in the place of a parent of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends to stand in the place of a parent of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: time the child spends in the care of a parent, of someone standing in a parent's
-- place or of someone who intends to, whether or not the child is physically with that person for
-- the whole of it. There is therefore no input about physical presence.
-- "decision-making responsibility" (src:931) has the meaning in subsection 2(1) of the Divorce Act,
-- which is not among the texts this piece reads: it is an input of "a child of a contributor" above.
-- out of range: subsection 2(1) of the Divorce Act (another statute, not among the inputs): the four facts are taken as given.
`s 42(1) — time that is a person's parenting time` `the child spends the time in the care of the person` `the person is a parent of the child` `the person stands in the place of a parent of the child` `the person intends to stand in the place of a parent of the child` MEANS
        `the child spends the time in the care of the person`
    AND (   `the person is a parent of the child`
         OR `the person stands in the place of a parent of the child`
         OR `the person intends to stand in the place of a parent of the child`)

-- src:932 | dependent child of a contributor means a child of the contributor who
-- src:933 | (a) is less than eighteen years of age,
-- src:934 | (b) is 18 or more years of age but less than 25 years of age and
-- src:935 | (i) is in full-time attendance at a school or university as defined by regulation, or
-- src:936 | (ii) is in part-time attendance at a school or university as defined by regulation, or
-- src:937 | (c) is a child other than a child described in paragraph (b), is eighteen or more years of age and is disabled, having been disabled without interruption since the time he reached eighteen years of age or the contributor died, whichever occurred later; (enfant à charge)
@ref Act s 42(1) "dependent child of a contributor" (src:932-937)
GIVEN `the individual is a child of the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the date on which it is asked whether the child is a dependent child` IS A DATE
      `the child is in full-time attendance at a school or university as defined by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child is in part-time attendance at a school or university as defined by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child is disabled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child has been disabled without interruption since the time the child reached eighteen years of age or the contributor died, whichever occurred later` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `cp3 Kind of dependent child`
-- Plain gloss: under 18; or 18 or more and under 25 and at school or university (full or part
-- time, as regulation 66 defines them, piece cr2); or, if not in (b), 18 or more and disabled without
-- a break since the later of turning 18 and the contributor's death.
-- The result says which paragraph, because the "disabled contributor's child" and the "orphan"
-- definitions leave out a child of paragraph (c).
-- out of range: regulation 66 (piece cr2): full-time and part-time attendance at a school or university are taken as facts.
`s 42(1) — the kind of dependent child that a child of a contributor is` `the individual is a child of the contributor` `the individual's date of birth` `the date on which it is asked whether the child is a dependent child` `the child is in full-time attendance at a school or university as defined by regulation` `the child is in part-time attendance at a school or university as defined by regulation` `the child is disabled` `the child has been disabled without interruption since the time the child reached eighteen years of age or the contributor died, whichever occurred later` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the individual is a child of the contributor`
                THEN `not a dependent child`
           IF NOT `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` `the individual's date of birth` 18 `the date on which it is asked whether the child is a dependent child`
                THEN `a dependent child under paragraph (a) of the definition`
           IF     NOT `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` `the individual's date of birth` 25 `the date on which it is asked whether the child is a dependent child`
              AND (   `the child is in full-time attendance at a school or university as defined by regulation`
                   OR `the child is in part-time attendance at a school or university as defined by regulation`)
                THEN `a dependent child under paragraph (b) of the definition`
           IF     `the child is disabled`
              AND `the child has been disabled without interruption since the time the child reached eighteen years of age or the contributor died, whichever occurred later`
                THEN `a dependent child under paragraph (c) of the definition`
           OTHERWISE `not a dependent child`

GIVEN kind IS A `cp3 Kind of dependent child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: any of the three paragraphs makes the child a dependent child.
`s 42(1) — a dependent child of a contributor` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `not a dependent child` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- src:938 | disabled contributor’s child or any form of that expression of like import means a dependent child of a contributor who is disabled, but does not include a dependent child described in paragraph (c) of the definition dependent child in this section; (enfant d’un cotisant invalide)
@ref Act s 42(1) "disabled contributor's child" (src:938)
GIVEN kind IS A `cp3 Kind of dependent child`
      `the contributor is disabled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a dependent child of a disabled contributor, but not one who is only a dependent child
-- by paragraph (c) of that definition.
`s 42(1) — a disabled contributor's child` kind `the contributor is disabled` MEANS
        `the contributor is disabled`
    AND (CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `a dependent child under paragraph (a) of the definition` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a dependent child under paragraph (b) of the definition` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

-- src:946 | orphan of a contributor means a dependent child of a contributor who has died but does not include a dependent child described in paragraph (c) of the definition dependent child; (orphelin)
@ref Act s 42(1) "orphan of a contributor" (src:946)
GIVEN kind IS A `cp3 Kind of dependent child`
      `the contributor has died` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a dependent child of a contributor who has died, but not one who is only a dependent
-- child by paragraph (c) of that definition.
`s 42(1) — an orphan of a contributor` kind `the contributor has died` MEANS
        `the contributor has died`
    AND (CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `a dependent child under paragraph (a) of the definition` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a dependent child under paragraph (b) of the definition` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

§§ `42(1) -- family allowance recipient`

-- src:939 | family allowance recipient means a person who received or is in receipt of an allowance or a family allowance pursuant to the Family Allowances Act, chapter F-1 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1970, as it read immediately before being repealed or the Family Allowances Act for that period prior to a child reaching seven years of age, and such other persons as may be prescribed by regulation; (bénéficiaire d’une allocation familiale)
@ref Act s 42(1) "family allowance recipient" (src:939)
GIVEN `the person received, or is in receipt of, an allowance or a family allowance under the Family Allowances Act for a period before a child reached seven years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is prescribed by regulation as a family allowance recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: someone who got the old family allowance for a child under seven, or whom a
-- regulation (regulation 77, piece cr2) names. The Family Allowances Act is not among the texts this
-- piece reads, so the first limb is a plain fact.
-- out of range: the Family Allowances Act (another statute, not among the inputs) and regulation 77 (piece cr2): both limbs are taken as facts.
`s 42(1) — a family allowance recipient` `the person received, or is in receipt of, an allowance or a family allowance under the Family Allowances Act for a period before a child reached seven years of age` `the person is prescribed by regulation as a family allowance recipient` MEANS
    `the person received, or is in receipt of, an allowance or a family allowance under the Family Allowances Act for a period before a child reached seven years of age` OR `the person is prescribed by regulation as a family allowance recipient`

§§ `42(1) -- Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average`

-- src:941 | (a) where the year is before 1998 or the date of birth of the contributor is before January 1, 1933, the two previous years, or
@ref Act s 42(1) "Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average" (src:941)
`s 42(1) "Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average" — the first day of 1933` MEANS YMD 1933 1 1

-- src:940 | Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, in respect of a contributor for a year, means the average of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year and
-- src:941 | (a) where the year is before 1998 or the date of birth of the contributor is before January 1, 1933, the two previous years, or
-- src:942 | (b) in any other case,
-- src:943 | (i) where the year is 1998, the three previous years, and
-- src:944 | (ii) where the year is after 1998, the four previous years; (maximum moyen des gains ouvrant droit à pension)
@ref Act s 42(1) "Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average" (src:940-944)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings of each year concerned` IS A LIST OF `cp3 Maximum pensionable earnings of a year`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: the average of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings of the year and of the two
-- previous years (a year before 1998, or a contributor born before 1933), of the three previous years
-- (the year 1998) or of the four previous years (a later year). Each figure is the value of section 18
-- (out of range: piece cp1) and is supplied in the list, one entry per year.
-- NOTHING means the list lacks a figure for one of the years concerned (or has two for one year).
-- out of range: section 18 (piece cp1): the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings of each year concerned is in the list.
`s 42(1) — the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for a year` year `the contributor's date of birth` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings of each year concerned` MEANS
    IF count `the figures of the years concerned` EQUALS (`the number of previous years` PLUS 1)
    THEN JUST ((sum (map (GIVEN f YIELD f's `Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings of that year`) `the figures of the years concerned`)) DIVIDED BY (`the number of previous years` PLUS 1))
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the number of previous years` MEANS
            BRANCH IF year LESS THAN 1998 OR `the contributor's date of birth` LESS THAN `s 42(1) "Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average" — the first day of 1933`
                        THEN 2
                   IF year EQUALS 1998 THEN 3
                   OTHERWISE 4
        `the figures of the years concerned` MEANS
            filter (GIVEN f YIELD    f's `calendar year of the figure` AT LEAST (year MINUS `the number of previous years`)
                                  AND f's `calendar year of the figure` AT MOST year)
                   `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings of each year concerned`

§§ `42(1) -- the Minister, substantially gainful, survivor, survivor with dependent children, wholly or substantially`

-- src:945 | Minister means the Minister of Employment and Social Development; (ministre)
@ref Act s 42(1) "Minister" (src:945)
GIVETH A Minister
-- Plain gloss: in Part II, the Minister is the Minister of Employment and Social Development.
`s 42(1) — the Minister of Part II` MEANS `the Minister of Employment and Social Development`

-- src:948 | substantially gainful, in respect of an occupation, has the meaning that may be prescribed; (véritablement rémunératrice)
@ref Act s 42(1) "substantially gainful" (src:948)
GIVEN `the occupation is substantially gainful as prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: the meaning "may be prescribed". Regulation 68.1 (piece cr2) prescribes it as an
-- occupation paying at least the maximum annual disability pension; that figure is out of range, so
-- whether an occupation meets it is a plain input.
-- out of range: regulation 68.1 (piece cr2): whether the occupation is substantially gainful as prescribed is taken as a fact.
`s 42(1) — an occupation is substantially gainful` `the occupation is substantially gainful as prescribed` MEANS
    `the occupation is substantially gainful as prescribed`

-- src:950 | survivor, in relation to a deceased contributor, means
-- src:951 | (a) if there is no person described in paragraph (b), a person who was married to the contributor at the time of the contributor’s death, or
-- src:952 | (b) a person who was the common-law partner of the contributor at the time of the contributor’s death; (survivant)
@ref Act s 42(1) "survivor" (src:950-952)
GIVEN `the person was the common-law partner of the contributor at the time of the contributor's death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was married to the contributor at the time of the contributor's death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person was the common-law partner of the contributor at the time of the contributor's death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: the common-law partner at the time of death; or, only if the contributor had no
-- common-law partner then, the person married to the contributor at the time of death.
-- Whether someone is a common-law partner at the death is `s 2(1) — a common-law partner of a
-- contributor at the contributor's death` in the core (cpp-core-definitions.l4).
`s 42(1) — a survivor of a deceased contributor` `the person was the common-law partner of the contributor at the time of the contributor's death` `the person was married to the contributor at the time of the contributor's death` `a person was the common-law partner of the contributor at the time of the contributor's death` MEANS
        `the person was the common-law partner of the contributor at the time of the contributor's death`
    OR  (    `the person was married to the contributor at the time of the contributor's death`
         AND NOT `a person was the common-law partner of the contributor at the time of the contributor's death`)

-- src:953 | survivor with dependent children means a survivor of a contributor who wholly or substantially maintains one or more dependent children of the contributor; (survivant avec enfant à charge)
-- src:954 | wholly or substantially has such meaning as may be prescribed. (entièrement ou dans une large mesure)
@ref Act s 42(1) "survivor with dependent children", "wholly or substantially" (src:953-954)
GIVEN `the person is a survivor of the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of dependent children of the contributor whom the survivor wholly or substantially maintains` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a survivor who wholly or substantially maintains at least one dependent child of the
-- deceased contributor. "Wholly or substantially" has the meaning that may be prescribed; regulation
-- 65 (piece cr2) says it is more than 50 per cent of the maintenance of those children, so the count
-- is of the children the survivor maintains in that sense.
-- out of range: regulation 65 (piece cr2): the count is of the dependent children the survivor maintains wholly or substantially.
`s 42(1) — a survivor with dependent children` `the person is a survivor of the contributor` `the number of dependent children of the contributor whom the survivor wholly or substantially maintains` MEANS
    `the person is a survivor of the contributor` AND `the number of dependent children of the contributor whom the survivor wholly or substantially maintains` AT LEAST 1

§§ `42(2) -- when a person is disabled, and from what time`

-- src:958 | (i) a disability is severe only if by reason thereof the person in respect of whom the determination is made is incapable regularly of pursuing any substantially gainful occupation, and
@ref Act s 42(2)(a)(i) (src:958)
GIVEN `the person is incapable regularly of pursuing any substantially gainful occupation by reason of the disability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a disability is severe only if the person cannot regularly pursue any substantially
-- gainful occupation because of it.
`s 42(2)(a)(i) — a disability is severe` `the person is incapable regularly of pursuing any substantially gainful occupation by reason of the disability` MEANS
    `the person is incapable regularly of pursuing any substantially gainful occupation by reason of the disability`

-- src:959 | (ii) a disability is prolonged only if it is determined in prescribed manner that the disability is likely to be long continued and of indefinite duration or is likely to result in death; and
@ref Act s 42(2)(a)(ii) (src:959)
GIVEN `it is determined in the prescribed manner that the disability is likely to be long continued and of indefinite duration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is determined in the prescribed manner that the disability is likely to result in death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a disability is prolonged only if it is determined, in the prescribed manner, to be
-- likely to be long continued and of indefinite duration, or likely to result in death.
`s 42(2)(a)(ii) — a disability is prolonged` `it is determined in the prescribed manner that the disability is likely to be long continued and of indefinite duration` `it is determined in the prescribed manner that the disability is likely to result in death` MEANS
    `it is determined in the prescribed manner that the disability is likely to be long continued and of indefinite duration` OR `it is determined in the prescribed manner that the disability is likely to result in death`

-- src:956 | (2) For the purposes of this Act,
-- src:957 | (a) a person shall be considered to be disabled only if he is determined in prescribed manner to have a severe and prolonged mental or physical disability, and for the purposes of this paragraph,
@ref Act s 42(2)(a) (src:956-957)
GIVEN `the person is determined in the prescribed manner to have a severe and prolonged mental or physical disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disability is severe` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disability is prolonged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a person is disabled only if determined, in the prescribed manner, to have a severe
-- and prolonged disability; the first input is that determination (a judgment the Act leaves to the
-- Minister, so it is a fact supplied conditionally), and the other two are the results of the two
-- rules above.
-- out of range: the prescribed manner of the determination (the Regulations, Part V: piece cr2) and the Minister's decision: taken as facts.
`s 42(2)(a) — a person is considered to be disabled` `the person is determined in the prescribed manner to have a severe and prolonged mental or physical disability` `the disability is severe` `the disability is prolonged` MEANS
    `the person is determined in the prescribed manner to have a severe and prolonged mental or physical disability` AND `the disability is severe` AND `the disability is prolonged`

-- src:960 | (b) a person is deemed to have become or to have ceased to be disabled at the time that is determined in the prescribed manner to be the time when the person became or ceased to be, as the case may be, disabled, but in no case shall a person — including a contributor referred to in subparagraph 44(1)(b)(ii) — be deemed to have become disabled earlier than fifteen months before the time of the making of any application in respect of which the determination is made.
@ref Act s 42(2)(b) (src:960)
GIVEN `the time determined in the prescribed manner to be the time when the person became disabled` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application in respect of which the determination is made was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
-- Plain gloss: the person is deemed to have become disabled at the time determined, but never earlier
-- than fifteen months before the application was made. The 15 months are counted back with the
-- core's `the date a time limit before a date goes back to`.
-- out of range: the prescribed manner of the determination (the Regulations, Part V: piece cr2): the time determined is taken as a fact.
`s 42(2)(b) — the time a person is deemed to have become disabled` `the time determined in the prescribed manner to be the time when the person became disabled` `the day on which the application in respect of which the determination is made was made` MEANS
    IF `the time determined in the prescribed manner to be the time when the person became disabled` AT LEAST `fifteen months before the application`
    THEN `the time determined in the prescribed manner to be the time when the person became disabled`
    ELSE `fifteen months before the application`
    WHERE
        `fifteen months before the application` MEANS
            `the date a time limit before a date goes back to` `the day on which the application in respect of which the determination is made was made` (`a number of months` WITH `number of months` IS 15)

-- src:960 | (b) a person is deemed to have become or to have ceased to be disabled at the time that is determined in the prescribed manner to be the time when the person became or ceased to be, as the case may be, disabled, but in no case shall a person — including a contributor referred to in subparagraph 44(1)(b)(ii) — be deemed to have become disabled earlier than fifteen months before the time of the making of any application in respect of which the determination is made.
@ref Act s 42(2)(b) (src:960)
GIVEN `the time determined in the prescribed manner to be the time when the person ceased to be disabled` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
-- Plain gloss: the fifteen-month limit is put on becoming disabled only; a person is deemed to have
-- ceased to be disabled at the time determined.
`s 42(2)(b) — the time a person is deemed to have ceased to be disabled` `the time determined in the prescribed manner to be the time when the person ceased to be disabled` MEANS
    `the time determined in the prescribed manner to be the time when the person ceased to be disabled`

§ `Part II -- The Pension Index (section 43)`

-- src:964 | 43 (1) Subject to subsection (2), the Pension Index for each year shall be calculated, in prescribed manner, as the average for the twelve month period ending October 31 in the preceding year of the Consumer Price Index for each month in that twelve month period.
@ref Act s 43(1) (src:964)
GIVEN `the Consumer Price Index for each month of the twelve month period ending October 31 in the preceding year` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: the Pension Index for a year is the average of the twelve monthly Consumer Price
-- Index figures of the twelve months ending on 31 October of the year before.
-- "In prescribed manner": regulation 75 (piece cr2) rounds the average to one decimal place; that
-- rounding is not done here (NOTES.md, fork register). NOTHING means the list is not twelve figures.
-- out of range: the Consumer Price Index (published by Statistics Canada, not among the inputs) and regulation 75 (piece cr2), which rounds the average.
`s 43(1) — the Pension Index for a year before the exception` `the Consumer Price Index for each month of the twelve month period ending October 31 in the preceding year` MEANS
    IF count `the Consumer Price Index for each month of the twelve month period ending October 31 in the preceding year` EQUALS 12
    THEN JUST ((sum `the Consumer Price Index for each month of the twelve month period ending October 31 in the preceding year`) DIVIDED BY 12)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:966 | (2) For any year for which the calculation required by subsection (1) yields a Pension Index that is less than the Pension Index for the preceding year, the Pension Index shall be taken to be the Pension Index for the preceding year.
@ref Act s 43(2) (src:966)
GIVEN `the Pension Index calculated under subsection (1) for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the Pension Index for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: the Pension Index never goes down: if the calculation gives less than last year's
-- index, last year's index is taken.
`s 43(2) — the Pension Index for a year` `the Pension Index calculated under subsection (1) for the year` `the Pension Index for the preceding year` MEANS
    max `the Pension Index calculated under subsection (1) for the year` `the Pension Index for the preceding year`

-- src:968 | (3) Where at any time the Consumer Price Index is adjusted to reflect a new time basis or a new content basis with a resulting percentage adjustment being made in the figures for that Index, a corresponding percentage adjustment shall, at the time of the next calculation of the Pension Index, be made in all values then existing of the Pension Index.
@ref Act s 43(3) (src:968)
GIVEN `a value of the Pension Index existing when the Consumer Price Index is rebased` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage adjustment made in the figures of the Consumer Price Index, as a fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: when the Consumer Price Index is rebased, with a percentage adjustment of its figures,
-- every Pension Index value then existing is adjusted by the same percentage at the next calculation.
-- A rise of 3 per cent is the fraction 0.03.
`s 43(3) — a value of the Pension Index after the Consumer Price Index is rebased` `a value of the Pension Index existing when the Consumer Price Index is rebased` `the percentage adjustment made in the figures of the Consumer Price Index, as a fraction` MEANS
    `a value of the Pension Index existing when the Consumer Price Index is rebased` TIMES (1 PLUS `the percentage adjustment made in the figures of the Consumer Price Index, as a fraction`)
